'dbtemplates_helpblurb' => "Custom databases created under the &quot;Databases&quot; heading require three templates to display various views of the database: a category template (which displays the database categories), a listing template (which displays the list of records in a category, or in the database), and a view template (which allows you to view a record).  You can use this page to create these various database templates for one or
		more databases.  You can use the same database templates for some or all of your databases, or create unique database templates for each database you use.<br /><br />
		You can create categories to organize your database templates.  You can drag'n'drop your database templates and categories to reorder them as you see fit.  You can export, edit and delete your database templates, and you can compare them to the default versions of the database template.<br /><br />
		When you edit a database template, the previous version is stored as a revision.  You can then edit, delete and restore the previous version if needed, and compare it to the current version of the database template to identify the differences between the two.<br /><br />
		Note that because database templates expect certain unique pieces of data to be supplied and displayed, there is an additional database variables help tab available in the template tag help panel to show you these variables.",
