'pagetemplates_helpblurb' => "Page templates allow you to define a common layout to be shared across multiple pages.  You can create page templates that act as a wrapper for your pages; when you add or edit a page in the &quot;Page Manager&quot; you can select a page template to use, and by default the page content you then define will be placed into your page template where the appropriate tag is used.<br /><br />
		You can also create true templates from here.  True templates are page templates that you select when creating a page, and the template is then imported to the page, allowing you to further customize and change it entirely (instead of it acting as a wrapper for the page you create).<br /><br />
		You can edit, delete and export page templates from this page.  You can also see which pages are using a given template (as a wrapper) by clicking the number shown next to &quot;Used by&quot;.<br /><br />
		When you edit a page template, the previous version is stored as a revision.  You can then edit, delete and restore the previous version if needed, and compare it to the current version of the page template to identify the differences between the two.",
